## **8. Understanding Gas and Transaction Fee**

This is an important part of the practical.

### **What is Gas?**

Gas is the unit used to measure the computational work required to execute operations on Ethereum.

### **What is Gas Price?**

Gas price is the amount paid for each unit of gas.

It is generally expressed in Gwei.

### **Formula**

\\[ \text{Transaction Fee} = \text{Gas Used}\times\text{Effective Gas Price} \\]

For example:

- Gas used = 50,000
- Gas price = 10 Gwei

\\[ 50000 \times 10 = 500000\ Gwei \\]

\\[ =0.0005\ ETH \\]

### **How to observe gas values**

After every transaction:

1. Open MetaMask activity.
2. Select the completed transaction.
3. Open the transaction details.
4. Note the gas used and transaction fee.
5. You can also open the transaction on the Sepolia Etherscan explorer.

[Sepolia Etherscan Explorer](https://sepolia.etherscan.io/?utm_source=chatgpt.com)

